@startuml 11b_crates_rust
!include ../style.iuml
title Package diagram: the Rust workspace (arrows are the path dependencies of each Cargo.toml)

package "rust/crates" {
  [cg-core] as CORE
  [cg-audit] as AUD
  [cg-engine] as ENG
  [cg-access] as ACC
  [cg-timestamp] as TS
  [cg-ingest] as ING
  [cg-queue] as Q
  [cg-mongo] as MG
  [cg-redis] as RD
  [cg-sim] as SIM
  [cg-api] as API
  [cg-cli] as CLI
}

AUD --> CORE
ENG --> CORE
ENG --> AUD
ACC --> CORE
ACC --> AUD
TS --> AUD
ING --> CORE
Q --> CORE
Q --> AUD
Q --> ACC
Q --> ENG
MG --> CORE
MG --> ACC
MG --> Q
RD --> Q
SIM --> Q
API --> CORE
API --> AUD
API --> ACC
API --> ENG
API --> Q
API --> TS
API --> ING
CLI --> CORE
CLI --> ENG
CLI --> AUD
CLI --> ACC
CLI --> API
CLI --> Q
CLI --> RD
CLI --> MG
CLI --> TS
CLI --> ING
CLI --> SIM

note bottom of CORE
  A crate never reaches up: the engine knows nothing of the web,
  the web layer nothing of the database. cg-core depends on no
  other crate. The database and the broker (cg-mongo, cg-redis)
  implement the store and broker contracts defined in cg-queue
  and cg-access; only cg-cli joins everything.
end note
@enduml
